<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">     (vi) Although there is clearly something going wrong in my code above that the LPE trajectory is wildly different, it still confirms my intuition that the LPE will be much smoother of an trajectory than converting.                Numerical error builds up in the conversion from r and v, and that oscullating behavior is shown in the red trajectory above. Although it is small, that oscullating behavior does not exist in the LPE-integrated                  trajectory of the eccentricity vector, an important characteristic as to why LPEs have advantages over cartesian.</Text-field>
</Input>
